From 3857140eac91f3880955538e053234e31b2148f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 11:53:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] treewide: replace removed strncpy() for Linux 7.2

Linux 7.2 removes strncpy() from the kernel (commit 079a028d6327
"string: Remove strncpy() from the kernel"), causing implicit-declaration
build errors. Replace every call site with the dedicated replacement:

  - strscpy_pad() for copies into NUL-terminated, zero-padded string
    fields (crypt.alg, net_device->name, old_ifname).
  - memcpy_and_pad() for the fixed-count / byte-append copies that must
    not truncate to a terminator (debug string builders, power-track
    token parsing, ParseQualifiedString, netlink ring names, WoWLAN
    pattern bytes, FW debug trace).

Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
